%U A263049 253253149671986953,134491669675212201371
%N A263049 a(n) = smallest prime prime(k) such that the gaps between the primes prime(k), prime(k+1), prime(k+2), ..., prime(k+n) are 2n, 2n-2, ... 6, 4, 2.
%C A263049 For a(16) the gap to the next primes are 32, 30, 28, 26, 24, 22, 20, 18, 16, 14, 12, 10, 8, 6, 4, 2.  The gap previous to a(16) is 10, and after the last gap of 2 is 48.
%C A263049 a(n) >= a(n-1) - 2n, because the pattern for a(n) has the pattern for a(n-1) starting at its second prime. Equality holds exactly when the prime before a(n-1) is a(n-1) - 2n, as for a(10) = a(9) - 20 and a(15) = a(14) - 30. So the sequence is not monotonic. - _Jeff Sponaugle_, Oct 06 2026
%e A263049 Consider the consecutive primes 1979, 1987, 1993, 1997, 1999. The gaps are 8, 6, 4, 2, and this does not occur for any prime smaller than 1979, so a(4)=1979.
%o A263049 (Python)
%o A263049 from collections import deque
%o A263049 from sympy import nextprime
%o A263049 def A263049(n):
%o A263049     d, p = deque([2], maxlen=n+1), 2
%o A263049     while True:
%o A263049         p = nextprime(p); d.append(p)
%o A263049         if len(d) > n and all(d[i+1]-d[i] == 2*(n-i) for i in range(n)): return d[0]
%o A263049 print([A263049(n) for n in range(1, 9)]) # _Jeff Sponaugle_, Oct 06 2026
